          <attvalue for="12" value="The Carnot cycle is described as a first approximation for the gas turbine engine due to its underlying assumptions." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="The assumptions made in the Carnot cycle make it only a first approximation for the gas turbine engine, particularly as additions of mass and heat are made to the working fluid via the burning of fuel." />
