          <attvalue for="11" value="INFLUENCES" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="The size of the grains in a material has an influence on the rates of fatigue crack growth." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="The influence of the grain size is very different when one considers the rates of fatigue crack growth and the creep rupture performance." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-1" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.012814645308924486" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.40768878718535473" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-e-3" id="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-r-2" weight="5.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="INFLUENCES" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="The size of the grains in a material has an influence on its creep rupture performance." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="The influence of the grain size is very different when one considers the rates of fatigue crack growth and the creep rupture performance." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-2" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.0008390541571319603" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.4005034324942792" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-e-6" id="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-r-4" weight="5.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="POSITIVELY_CORRELATES_WITH" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="A larger grain size of 360 µm resulted in a longer rupture life of approximately 600 h, whereas a smaller grain size of 19 µm resulted in a shorter rupture life of about 200 h." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="for the largest grain size of 360 µm, the rupture life approached 600 h under these conditions, but at 19 µm it decreased to about 200 h." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-4" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.0008390541571319603" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.4005034324942792" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-e-7" id="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654-r-5" weight="4.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="HAS_SIMILAR_INFLUENCE_ON" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="The influence of grain size on material properties observed by Bain et al. is similar to observations made in the NR3 superalloy." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="Similar observations have been made [25] in the NR3 superalloy" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-5" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-9b97021f9b9b8256b6c78711278f4654" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.26666666666666666" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-8827e315f10ef4c6612df3e85c9f593c-e-1" id="chunk-8827e315f10ef4c6612df3e85c9f593c-r-6" weight="5.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="INFLUENCED" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="The grain size had a considerable effect on the crack growth rate, which was about two orders of magnitude smaller for larger grain sizes, particularly at 650°C." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="Particularly at the higher temperature, the dependence of crack growth rate on grain size was considerable (see Figure 4.32), being about two orders of magnitude smaller for the larger grain size" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-6" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-8827e315f10ef4c6612df3e85c9f593c" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.005606407322654463" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.4033638443935927" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-c5e3ecc2944d1e5e7853c5fa9484d5fa-e-4" id="chunk-c5e3ecc2944d1e5e7853c5fa9484d5fa-r-4" weight="5.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="DOES_NOT_INFLUENCE" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="Grain size did not heavily influence the Paris exponents." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="However, at both temperatures, the Paris exponents in stage II growth were not heavily influenced by grain size." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-4" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-c5e3ecc2944d1e5e7853c5fa9484d5fa" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.0016781083142639206" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.40100686498855836" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-100afba087a43fc5308b3284aa10cb35-e-5" id="chunk-100afba087a43fc5308b3284aa10cb35-r-5" weight="4.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="IS_PARAMETER_FOR" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="Grain size is a controlled parameter when comparing the ultrasonic inspectability of different materials." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="Interestingly, for any given grain size, powder metallurgy (P/M) material exhibits ultrasonic inspectability which is very much better than for conventional cast-and-wrought product." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-5" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-100afba087a43fc5308b3284aa10cb35" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.0007627765064836003" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.26712433257055684" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-821a3f267f9ff96b58c19914c2c7eff8-e-1" id="chunk-821a3f267f9ff96b58c19914c2c7eff8-r-4" weight="5.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="REDUCES" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="Reducing the grain size has been found to reduce the thermal conductivity." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="Reducing the grain size has also been found to reduce the thermal conductivity [56] (see Figure 5.20)" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-4" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-821a3f267f9ff96b58c19914c2c7eff8" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.4" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
      <edge source="chunk-c170c36341964554c175d2ca279d86c6-e-10" target="chunk-024c36ea3394fc7ba3bfdd8df0168497-e-1" id="chunk-024c36ea3394fc7ba3bfdd8df0168497-r-4" weight="4.0">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="STRENGTHENS" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="Strengthening is imparted to superalloy turbine discs by controlling grain size." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="hence, great emphasis has been placed on imparting strengthening by grain size and precipitation hardening due to the y' phase." />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-4" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-024c36ea3394fc7ba3bfdd8df0168497" />
          <attvalue for="17" value="0.26666666666666666" />
        </attvalues>
      </edge>
