          <attvalue for="13" value="...it was confirmed that in Ni–Cr–Al ternary alloys, and depending upon the precise mean composition, either an alumina (Al2O3) or a chromia (Cr2O3) oxide scale can form exclusively during exposure to high temperatures..." />
