        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="11" value="HAS_DEPENDENCE" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="The critical resolved shear stress (τc) is proportional to the square root of the particle radius (r), as shown by the approximation τc ∝ (fr)¹/²." />
          <attvalue for="13" value="Thus, significant fractions of larger particles are expected to promote hardening. Data [48] for the age hardening of monocrystalline Ni–Al alloys tested in compression have confirmed the r¹/² dependence expected as f → 0" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="r-1" />
          <attvalue for="15" value="chunk-c026408b0eb125d3c56d1ed05d0a0f15" />
          <attvalue for="16" value="0.0006747638326585695" />
